    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-58e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58E Production to the Tribunal of certain exempt documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-1-sec-58e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In any proceedings before the Tribunal under this Act in relation to\na document that is claimed to be an exempt document under\nsection 33 or 34, the Tribunal is entitled to require the production\nof the document in accordance with this section and not in\naccordance with section 64, section 37 of the Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975 or otherwise.\n\n(2) If the Tribunal is not satisfied by evidence on affidavit or otherwise\nthat the document is an exempt document under section 33 or 34,\nthe Tribunal may require the document to be produced for\ninspection by the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of the\nproceeding.\n\n(3) If, after an inspection of a document under this section, the\nTribunal is satisfied that the document is an exempt document, the\nTribunal must return the document to the person by whom it was\nproduced without permitting a person to have access to the\ndocument or disclosing the contents of the document to a person,\nunless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 60A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In any proceedings before the Tribunal under this Act in relation to\na document that is claimed to be an exempt document under\nsection 33 or 34, the Tribunal is entitled to require the production\nof the document in accordance with this section and not in\naccordance with section 64, section 37 of the Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975 or otherwise.\n\n(2) If the Tribunal is not satisfied by evidence on affidavit or otherwise\nthat the document is an exempt document under section 33 or 34,\nthe Tribunal may require the document to be produced for\ninspection by the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of the\nproceeding.\n\n(3) If, after an inspection of a document under this section, the\nTribunal is satisfied that the document is an exempt document, the\nTribunal must return the document to the person by whom it was\nproduced without permitting a person to have access to the\ndocument or disclosing the contents of the document to a person,\nunless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 60A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-58e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-58e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-58e-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "60573d73f7fa735907f9d5bec79d4164bcda81d4858bbd357e142184ef5f3a4e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-1-sec-58e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58E Production to the Tribunal of certain exempt documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In any proceedings before the Tribunal under this Act in relation to\na document that is claimed to be an exempt document under\nsection 33 or 34, the Tribunal is entitled to require the production\nof the document in accordance with this section and not in\naccordance with section 64, section 37 of the Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975 or otherwise.\n\n(2) If the Tribunal is not satisfied by evidence on affidavit or otherwise\nthat the document is an exempt document under section 33 or 34,\nthe Tribunal may require the document to be produced for\ninspection by the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of the\nproceeding.\n\n(3) If, after an inspection of a document under this section, the\nTribunal is satisfied that the document is an exempt document, the\nTribunal must return the document to the person by whom it was\nproduced without permitting a person to have access to the\ndocument or disclosing the contents of the document to a person,\nunless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 60A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security."
    },
