    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2009 No. 99, 2009",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-1-sec-2009-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975, the Tribunal must:\n\n(a) have regard to:\n\n(i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof exempt matter contained in a document to which the\nproceedings relate; and\n\n(ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof information of the kind referred to in subsection\n25(1); and\n\n(b) where the proceedings relate to a document that is claimed to\nbe an exempt document under section 33—give particular\nweight to a submission made by an agency or a Minister that\nit is desirable to make the order or orders under subsection\n35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975\nbecause disclosure of the document:\n\n(i) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause\ndamage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an\nauthority of a foreign government or an international\norganisation to the Government of the Commonwealth,\nto an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person\nreceiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975, the Tribunal must:\n\n(a) have regard to:\n\n(i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof exempt matter contained in a document to which the\nproceedings relate; and\n\n(ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof information of the kind referred to in subsection\n25(1); and\n\n(b) where the proceedings relate to a document that is claimed to\nbe an exempt document under section 33—give particular\nweight to a submission made by an agency or a Minister that\nit is desirable to make the order or orders under subsection\n35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975\nbecause disclosure of the document:\n\n(i) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause\ndamage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an\nauthority of a foreign government or an international\norganisation to the Government of the Commonwealth,\nto an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person\nreceiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ff17156e91a201c4e3f115e285af340aa587ebbd247d224b355ac1085e6a034",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal must consider certain factors when deciding whether to make an order under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-1-sec-2009-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2009 No. 99, 2009",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975, the Tribunal must:\n\n(a) have regard to:\n\n(i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof exempt matter contained in a document to which the\nproceedings relate; and\n\n(ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof information of the kind referred to in subsection\n25(1); and\n\n(b) where the proceedings relate to a document that is claimed to\nbe an exempt document under section 33—give particular\nweight to a submission made by an agency or a Minister that\nit is desirable to make the order or orders under subsection\n35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975\nbecause disclosure of the document:\n\n(i) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause\ndamage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(ii) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an\nauthority of a foreign government or an international\norganisation to the Government of the Commonwealth,\nto an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person\nreceiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the\nCommonwealth."
    },
