    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Subsection 64(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-1-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Section 37 of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 does\nnot apply in relation to a document that is claimed to be an exempt\ndocument, but in proceedings before the Tribunal in relation to\nsuch a document, the Tribunal may, for the purpose of deciding\nwhether the document is an exempt document, require the\ndocument to be produced for inspection by members of the\nTribunal only.\n\nFreedom of Information Act 1982  Schedule 1\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            11\n\n(1AA) If, upon the inspection, the Tribunal is satisfied that the document\nis an exempt document, the Tribunal must return the document to\nthe person by whom it was produced without permitting a person\nto have access to the document, or disclosing the contents of the\ndocument to a person, unless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 60A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Section 37 of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 does\nnot apply in relation to a document that is claimed to be an exempt\ndocument, but in proceedings before the Tribunal in relation to\nsuch a document, the Tribunal may, for the purpose of deciding\nwhether the document is an exempt document, require the\ndocument to be produced for inspection by members of the\nTribunal only.\n\nFreedom of Information Act 1982  Schedule 1\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            11\n\n(1AA) If, upon the inspection, the Tribunal is satisfied that the document\nis an exempt document, the Tribunal must return the document to\nthe person by whom it was produced without permitting a person\nto have access to the document, or disclosing the contents of the\ndocument to a person, unless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 60A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-28-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-28-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "939ebf4bb6337145bbc31ccccb66701b28ceedffc225ef3b7d5ee79aa7ff6a54",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal may require document production for inspection, but not disclosure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-1-sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Subsection 64(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Section 37 of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 does\nnot apply in relation to a document that is claimed to be an exempt\ndocument, but in proceedings before the Tribunal in relation to\nsuch a document, the Tribunal may, for the purpose of deciding\nwhether the document is an exempt document, require the\ndocument to be produced for inspection by members of the\nTribunal only.\n\nFreedom of Information Act 1982  Schedule 1\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            11\n\n(1AA) If, upon the inspection, the Tribunal is satisfied that the document\nis an exempt document, the Tribunal must return the document to\nthe person by whom it was produced without permitting a person\nto have access to the document, or disclosing the contents of the\ndocument to a person, unless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 60A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-28-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
