        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nArchives Act 1983  Schedule 2\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            15\n\n(1) If an application is made to the Tribunal for review of a decision\nrefusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an\napplication under section 40, being a record that is:\n\n(a) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains\ninformation or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(b) not a record of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation;\nthen the Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with\nsubsection (2) for the purposes of any proceeding in relation to the\napplication.\nNote:\nSection 21AB of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975\ncontains the requirements for constitution of the Tribunal in\nproceedings about a record of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that\nit contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b).\nNote:\nThe heading to section 46 is replaced by the heading “Constitution of Tribunal for\nproceedings about certain exempt records”.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nArchives Act 1983  Schedule 2\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            15\n\n(1) If an application is made to the Tribunal for review of a decision\nrefusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an\napplication under section 40, being a record that is:\n\n(a) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains\ninformation or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(b) not a record of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation;\nthen the Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with\nsubsection (2) for the purposes of any proceeding in relation to the\napplication.\nNote:\nSection 21AB of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975\ncontains the requirements for constitution of the Tribunal in\nproceedings about a record of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that\nit contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b).\nNote:\nThe heading to section 46 is replaced by the heading “Constitution of Tribunal for\nproceedings about certain exempt records”.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b074d0e881d425f4b2655895a6fb30a606607ba93d6606aeb8300740ae968a0",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with subsection (2) for proceedings about certain exempt records."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Subsection 46(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\nArchives Act 1983  Schedule 2\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            15\n\n(1) If an application is made to the Tribunal for review of a decision\nrefusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an\napplication under section 40, being a record that is:\n\n(a) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains\ninformation or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(b) not a record of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation;\nthen the Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with\nsubsection (2) for the purposes of any proceeding in relation to the\napplication.\nNote:\nSection 21AB of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975\ncontains the requirements for constitution of the Tribunal in\nproceedings about a record of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that\nit contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b).\nNote:\nThe heading to section 46 is replaced by the heading “Constitution of Tribunal for\nproceedings about certain exempt records”."
    },
