    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide evidence on potential breach of confidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Before determining that the record is not an exempt record, the Tribunal must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...whether making the record available for public access would constitute a breach of confidence by disclosing information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50A(3) Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-50a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before determining that part of, or a copy of part of, the record is\nto be made available for public access under section 38, the\nTribunal must request the Inspector-General to appear personally\nand give evidence on:\n\n(a) whether making that part, or a copy of that part, of the record\navailable for public access could reasonably be expected to\ncause damage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(b) whether making that part, or a copy of that part, of the record\navailable for public access would constitute a breach of\nconfidence by disclosing information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n\nArchives Act 1983  Schedule 2\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            17",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Before determining that part of, or a copy of part of, the record is\nto be made available for public access under section 38, the\nTribunal must request the Inspector-General to appear personally\nand give evidence on:\n\n(a) whether making that part, or a copy of that part, of the record\navailable for public access could reasonably be expected to\ncause damage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(b) whether making that part, or a copy of that part, of the record\navailable for public access would constitute a breach of\nconfidence by disclosing information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n\nArchives Act 1983  Schedule 2\n\nFreedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 99, 2009            17",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
