      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Tribunal has a cognitive task to perform",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Archives and Commonwealth institutions' evidence must be processed cognitively by Tribunal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50A(5) Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-50a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Inspector-General must comply with a request under\nsubsection (2) or (3) unless, in the opinion of the\nInspector-General, the Inspector-General is not appropriately\nqualified to give evidence on the matters in relation to which the\nInspector-General has been requested to give evidence.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The Inspector-General must comply with a request under\nsubsection (2) or (3) unless, in the opinion of the\nInspector-General, the Inspector-General is not appropriately\nqualified to give evidence on the matters in relation to which the\nInspector-General has been requested to give evidence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-5-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f55350be52b4769164f20b6cd4a0dcfc7b1989a0e34ed2dd3a60f449ab9545e",
      "skos:note": "Inspector-General must comply with a request unless not appropriately qualified."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-50a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50A(5) Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Inspector-General must comply with a request under\nsubsection (2) or (3) unless, in the opinion of the\nInspector-General, the Inspector-General is not appropriately\nqualified to give evidence on the matters in relation to which the\nInspector-General has been requested to give evidence."
    },
    {
