      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50A(6) Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-50a-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of enabling the Inspector-General to comply with\na request under subsection (2) or (3):\n\n(a) the Tribunal must allow the Inspector-General to take\npossession of, and make copies of or take extracts from, any\nrecord given to the Tribunal for the purposes of the\nproceeding; and\n\n(b) the Inspector-General may require the production of the\nrecord that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason\nthat it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in\nparagraph 33(1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(c) the Inspector-General may require the production of any\nCommonwealth record that relates to the record mentioned in\nparagraph (b); and\n\n(d) the Inspector-General may make copies of, or take extracts,\nfrom the records mentioned in paragraphs (b) and (c); and\n\n(e) after such period as is reasonably necessary for the purposes\nof giving evidence to the Tribunal, the Inspector-General\nmust:\n\n(i) return the original of any record to the Tribunal or to the\nentity that produced the record; and\n\n(ii) destroy any copies of or extracts taken from any record.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) For the purposes of enabling the Inspector-General to comply with\na request under subsection (2) or (3):\n\n(a) the Tribunal must allow the Inspector-General to take\npossession of, and make copies of or take extracts from, any\nrecord given to the Tribunal for the purposes of the\nproceeding; and\n\n(b) the Inspector-General may require the production of the\nrecord that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason\nthat it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in\nparagraph 33(1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(c) the Inspector-General may require the production of any\nCommonwealth record that relates to the record mentioned in\nparagraph (b); and\n\n(d) the Inspector-General may make copies of, or take extracts,\nfrom the records mentioned in paragraphs (b) and (c); and\n\n(e) after such period as is reasonably necessary for the purposes\nof giving evidence to the Tribunal, the Inspector-General\nmust:\n\n(i) return the original of any record to the Tribunal or to the\nentity that produced the record; and\n\n(ii) destroy any copies of or extracts taken from any record.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e3b9a4566174cae36b143654217d39ab6d19ecad2f859b7a8a685226c8cb4a4c",
      "skos:note": "The Tribunal must allow the Inspector-General to take possession of records.",
      "dc:description": "Tribunal must provide records for inspection"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-50a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50A(6) Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of enabling the Inspector-General to comply with\na request under subsection (2) or (3):\n\n(a) the Tribunal must allow the Inspector-General to take\npossession of, and make copies of or take extracts from, any\nrecord given to the Tribunal for the purposes of the\nproceeding; and\n\n(b) the Inspector-General may require the production of the\nrecord that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason\nthat it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in\nparagraph 33(1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(c) the Inspector-General may require the production of any\nCommonwealth record that relates to the record mentioned in\nparagraph (b); and\n\n(d) the Inspector-General may make copies of, or take extracts,\nfrom the records mentioned in paragraphs (b) and (c); and\n\n(e) after such period as is reasonably necessary for the purposes\nof giving evidence to the Tribunal, the Inspector-General\nmust:\n\n(i) return the original of any record to the Tribunal or to the\nentity that produced the record; and\n\n(ii) destroy any copies of or extracts taken from any record."
    },
