    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Subsection 52(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 for the purposes of\nproceedings in relation to an application under section 43, the\nTribunal must:\n\n(a) have regard to:\n\n(i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof matter contained in a record to which the proceedings\nrelate, being matter by reason of which the record is an\nexempt record; and\n\n(ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof information of the kind referred to in subsection\n39(1); and\n\n(b) where the proceedings relate to a record that is claimed to be\nan exempt record for the reason that it contains information\nor matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b)—\ngive particular weight to a submission made by the Archives\nthat it is desirable to make the order or orders under\nsubsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act\n1975 because the record contains information or matter of\nthat kind.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 for the purposes of\nproceedings in relation to an application under section 43, the\nTribunal must:\n\n(a) have regard to:\n\n(i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof matter contained in a record to which the proceedings\nrelate, being matter by reason of which the record is an\nexempt record; and\n\n(ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof information of the kind referred to in subsection\n39(1); and\n\n(b) where the proceedings relate to a record that is claimed to be\nan exempt record for the reason that it contains information\nor matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b)—\ngive particular weight to a submission made by the Archives\nthat it is desirable to make the order or orders under\nsubsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act\n1975 because the record contains information or matter of\nthat kind.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-11-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-11-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e857ea514ef366aa002aa9e4bbfb1b800ff0e2ff1fb9e8ca7fd1aa0fe7e41212",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal must consider certain factors when deciding to make an order under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Subsection 52(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 for the purposes of\nproceedings in relation to an application under section 43, the\nTribunal must:\n\n(a) have regard to:\n\n(i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof matter contained in a record to which the proceedings\nrelate, being matter by reason of which the record is an\nexempt record; and\n\n(ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant\nof information of the kind referred to in subsection\n39(1); and\n\n(b) where the proceedings relate to a record that is claimed to be\nan exempt record for the reason that it contains information\nor matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b)—\ngive particular weight to a submission made by the Archives\nthat it is desirable to make the order or orders under\nsubsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act\n1975 because the record contains information or matter of\nthat kind."
    },
    {
