    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 Subsection 53(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Section 37 of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 does\nnot apply in relation to a record that is claimed to be an exempt\nrecord, but in proceedings before the Tribunal in relation to such a\nrecord, if the Tribunal is not satisfied, by evidence on affidavit or\notherwise, that the record is an exempt record, it may require the\nrecord to be produced for inspection by members of the Tribunal\nonly.\n\n(1A) If, upon the inspection, the Tribunal is satisfied that the record is an\nexempt record, the Tribunal must return the record to the person by\nwhom it was produced without permitting a person to have access\nto the record, or disclosing the contents of the record to a person,\nunless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 50A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Section 37 of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 does\nnot apply in relation to a record that is claimed to be an exempt\nrecord, but in proceedings before the Tribunal in relation to such a\nrecord, if the Tribunal is not satisfied, by evidence on affidavit or\notherwise, that the record is an exempt record, it may require the\nrecord to be produced for inspection by members of the Tribunal\nonly.\n\n(1A) If, upon the inspection, the Tribunal is satisfied that the record is an\nexempt record, the Tribunal must return the record to the person by\nwhom it was produced without permitting a person to have access\nto the record, or disclosing the contents of the record to a person,\nunless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 50A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-13-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-13-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13 Subsection 53(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Section 37 of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 does\nnot apply in relation to a record that is claimed to be an exempt\nrecord, but in proceedings before the Tribunal in relation to such a\nrecord, if the Tribunal is not satisfied, by evidence on affidavit or\notherwise, that the record is an exempt record, it may require the\nrecord to be produced for inspection by members of the Tribunal\nonly.\n\n(1A) If, upon the inspection, the Tribunal is satisfied that the record is an\nexempt record, the Tribunal must return the record to the person by\nwhom it was produced without permitting a person to have access\nto the record, or disclosing the contents of the record to a person,\nunless the person is:\n\n(a) a member of the Tribunal as constituted for the purposes of\nthe proceeding; or\n\n(b) a member of the staff of the Tribunal in the course of the\nperformance of his or her duties as a member of that staff; or\n\n(c) in the circumstances permitted under paragraph 50A(6)(a)—\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security."
    },
