    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55A Automatic stay of certain decisions on appeal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-55a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person applies, under section 43, to the Tribunal for review\nof a decision refusing to make a record that is claimed to be\nan exempt record available for public access; and\n\n(b) the Tribunal decides that a person may have access to the\nrecord, or part of the record; and\n\n(c) the Archives institutes an appeal to the Federal Court of\nAustralia from the decision of the Tribunal.\n\n(2) If this section applies to a decision of the Tribunal, the operation of\nthe decision is stayed by force of this section from the time at\nwhich the appeal is instituted.\n\n(3) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the\ndecision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is\ndetermined by the Federal Court of Australia, the stay continues to\nhave effect until the earlier of:\n\n(a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Court of\nAustralia on the appeal takes effect; and\n\n(b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Court of\nAustralia.\n\n(4) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the\ndecision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is\ndetermined by the Federal Magistrates Court, the stay continues to\nhave effect until the earlier of:\n\n(a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Magistrates\nCourt on the appeal takes effect; and\n\n(b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Magistrates\nCourt.\n\n(5) Nothing in this section affects the power of the Federal Court of\nAustralia or the Federal Magistrates Court to make orders under\nsection 44A of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 in\nrelation to matters other than staying the decision of the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person applies, under section 43, to the Tribunal for review\nof a decision refusing to make a record that is claimed to be\nan exempt record available for public access; and\n\n(b) the Tribunal decides that a person may have access to the\nrecord, or part of the record; and\n\n(c) the Archives institutes an appeal to the Federal Court of\nAustralia from the decision of the Tribunal.\n\n(2) If this section applies to a decision of the Tribunal, the operation of\nthe decision is stayed by force of this section from the time at\nwhich the appeal is instituted.\n\n(3) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the\ndecision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is\ndetermined by the Federal Court of Australia, the stay continues to\nhave effect until the earlier of:\n\n(a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Court of\nAustralia on the appeal takes effect; and\n\n(b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Court of\nAustralia.\n\n(4) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the\ndecision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is\ndetermined by the Federal Magistrates Court, the stay continues to\nhave effect until the earlier of:\n\n(a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Magistrates\nCourt on the appeal takes effect; and\n\n(b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Magistrates\nCourt.\n\n(5) Nothing in this section affects the power of the Federal Court of\nAustralia or the Federal Magistrates Court to make orders under\nsection 44A of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 in\nrelation to matters other than staying the decision of the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f1581249676c89bdebdd7511d316cfd205843f8e897697ae101f76dd7fb6825"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-55a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55A Automatic stay of certain decisions on appeal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person applies, under section 43, to the Tribunal for review\nof a decision refusing to make a record that is claimed to be\nan exempt record available for public access; and\n\n(b) the Tribunal decides that a person may have access to the\nrecord, or part of the record; and\n\n(c) the Archives institutes an appeal to the Federal Court of\nAustralia from the decision of the Tribunal.\n\n(2) If this section applies to a decision of the Tribunal, the operation of\nthe decision is stayed by force of this section from the time at\nwhich the appeal is instituted.\n\n(3) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the\ndecision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is\ndetermined by the Federal Court of Australia, the stay continues to\nhave effect until the earlier of:\n\n(a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Court of\nAustralia on the appeal takes effect; and\n\n(b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Court of\nAustralia.\n\n(4) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the\ndecision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is\ndetermined by the Federal Magistrates Court, the stay continues to\nhave effect until the earlier of:\n\n(a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Magistrates\nCourt on the appeal takes effect; and\n\n(b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Magistrates\nCourt.\n\n(5) Nothing in this section affects the power of the Federal Court of\nAustralia or the Federal Magistrates Court to make orders under\nsection 44A of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 in\nrelation to matters other than staying the decision of the Tribunal."
    },
