    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-3-sec-21ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21AB Constitution of Security Appeals Division—proceedings to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-3-sec-21ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "review certain decisions under the Archives Act 1983\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to a proceeding in the Security Appeals\nDivision in relation to a review of a decision of the Australian\nArchives under the Archives Act 1983 refusing to grant access to a\nrecord in accordance with an application under section 40 of that\nAct, being a record that is:\n\n(a) a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation;\nand\n\n(b) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains\ninformation or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b) of that Act.\nConstitution of Security Appeals Division\n\n(2) Subject to this section, the Security Appeals Division is to be\nconstituted by:\n\n(a) 3 presidential members; or\n\n(b) a presidential member alone.\nWhen presidential member must not participate\n\n(3) A presidential member must not participate in the proceeding if he\nor she is, or has been, the Director-General of Security or an\n\nSchedule 3  Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975",
      "skos:definition": "review certain decisions under the Archives Act 1983\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to a proceeding in the Security Appeals\nDivision in relation to a review of a decision of the Australian\nArchives under the Archives Act 1983 refusing to grant access to a\nrecord in accordance with an application under section 40 of that\nAct, being a record that is:\n\n(a) a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation;\nand\n\n(b) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains\ninformation or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph\n33(1)(a) or (b) of that Act.\nConstitution of Security Appeals Division\n\n(2) Subject to this section, the Security Appeals Division is to be\nconstituted by:\n\n(a) 3 presidential members; or\n\n(b) a presidential member alone.\nWhen presidential member must not participate\n\n(3) A presidential member must not participate in the proceeding if he\nor she is, or has been, the Director-General of Security or an\n\nSchedule 3  Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-3-sec-21ab-ss-1"
